### =====================================================================
### END-TO-END (Phase 11): platform settings, reviews and ratings, invoices, reports - through the gateway (8080)
###
###   A. The super admin changes the delivery fee and minimum order -> cart-service uses them (PlatformSettingsChanged);
###      banners and feature flags; the audit log
###   B. An order is delivered -> PDF invoice, product review (rating shows in search), delivery rating
###   C. The admin dashboard, sales reports, top lists and the super admin's commission report
###   D. Put the settings back (other e2e files expect delivery fee 30.00 and minimum order 99.00)
###
### Needs: every service (Phases 1-11) + the connectors (scripts\register-connectors.ps1).
### Written for the VS Code "REST Client" extension. Run the requests IN ORDER.
### =====================================================================

@gatewayUrl = http://localhost:8080
@today = {{$datetime "YYYY-MM-DD"}}

@customerToken = {{customerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@vendorToken = {{vendorLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@adminToken = {{adminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@superAdminToken = {{superAdminLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@partnerToken = {{partnerLogin.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}
@orderId = {{order.response.body.$.data.id}}
@deliveryId = {{partnerDelivery.response.body.$.data.content[0].id}}
@reviewId = {{review.response.body.$.data.id}}


### 1. customer1 (user 4) logs in
# @name customerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 2. vendor1 (Fresh Mart) logs in
# @name vendorLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "vendor1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 3. The admin logs in
# @name adminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 4. The super admin logs in
# @name superAdminLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "superadmin@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### 5. delivery1 logs in
# @name partnerLogin
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "delivery1@grocery.com",
  "password": "Password@123"
}


### ===== A. Platform settings, banners, feature flags =====

### 6. Public settings (no login): INR, delivery fee 30.00, free from 299.00, minimum order 99.00
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/platform/settings


### 7. Public feature flags (no login)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/platform/feature-flags


### 8. Home page banners (no login): the expired Diwali banner is not shown
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/banners


### 9. An admin cannot change platform settings -> 403
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "INR",
  "deliveryFee": 25.00,
  "freeDeliveryFrom": 249.00,
  "minimumOrderValue": 79.00,
  "supportEmail": "support@grocery.com",
  "supportPhone": "1800-123-4567"
}


### 10. The super admin lowers the delivery fee and the minimum order (PlatformSettingsChanged)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "INR",
  "deliveryFee": 25.00,
  "freeDeliveryFrom": 249.00,
  "minimumOrderValue": 79.00,
  "supportEmail": "support@grocery.com",
  "supportPhone": "1800-123-4567"
}


### 11. customer1 starts with an empty cart
DELETE {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 12. (wait) ...adds 2 kg of tomatoes (72.00): cart-service already uses the new rules -> delivery 25.00, minimum 79.00
# @wait 3
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}


### 13. ...and 1 Amul Taaza Toned Milk (27.00) -> 99.00, above the new minimum
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/cart/items
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 6,
  "quantity": 1
}


### 14. The admin adds a banner
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/banners
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Weekend fruit festival",
  "subtitle": "Up to 20 % off fruits",
  "imageUrl": "http://localhost:8080/media/banners/fruits.jpg",
  "linkUrl": "/categories/2",
  "position": 3,
  "active": true
}


### 15. The home page now shows it too
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/banners


### 16. The super admin switches on delivery slots
PATCH {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/feature-flags/DELIVERY_SLOTS
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": true
}


### 17. Audit log: who changed what (settings, flags and banners are recorded here)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/audit-log?source=platform-service&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}


### 18. Audit log: everything that happened to customer1 (events of every service)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/audit-log?userId=4&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}


### ===== B. Deliver an order -> invoice, review, delivery rating =====

### 19. customer1 orders COD (99.00 + 25.00 delivery)
# @name order
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "addressId": 1,
  "paymentMethod": "COD"
}


### 20. No invoice before the store accepts -> 400
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 21. vendor1 accepts it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 22. ...prints the invoice to put in the bag (PDF)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 23. ...packs it
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/pack
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 24. ...and hands it over
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/orders/{{orderId}}/ready-for-pickup
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 25. (wait) delivery1 goes online -> gets the delivery
# @wait 3
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/online
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 26. delivery1's current delivery
# @name partnerDelivery
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries?active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 27. accept
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 28. pick up
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/pick-up
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 29. start
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/start
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 30. deliver
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/deliveries/{{deliveryId}}/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 31. (wait) The customer downloads the tax invoice (PDF)
# @wait 4
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}


### 32. customer1 reviews the tomatoes of this order: 4 stars
# @name review
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 4,
  "comment": "Fresh and firm, one was a bit soft"
}


### 33. The same product of the same order again -> 409
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 5
}


### 34. A product that was not in the order -> 400
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/9/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 5
}


### 35. Everybody can read the reviews of a product (no login)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/1/reviews


### 36. (wait) Search shows the new average rating (product-service -> Debezium -> Elasticsearch)
# @wait 3
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products/1


### 37. Best rated products first
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/products?sort=RATING&size=3


### 38. customer1 rates the delivery: 5 stars
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery-ratings
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": {{orderId}},
  "rating": 5,
  "comment": "Very polite, on time"
}


### 39. delivery1 sees the rating in the profile
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}


### 40. vendor1 reads the reviews of the store's products
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/reviews
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 41. The admin hides a review (it no longer counts for the rating)
PATCH {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reviews/{{reviewId}}/hide
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "reason": "Test review"
}


### ===== C. Reports (built by report-service from the events) =====

### 42. (wait) Admin dashboard
# @wait 2
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reports/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 43. Sales per day (today)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reports/sales/daily?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 44. Best-selling products this period
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reports/top-products?from={{today}}&to={{today}}&limit=5
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 45. Stores with the highest sales
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reports/top-stores?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}


### 46. vendor1: the daily sales of Fresh Mart
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/vendor/reports/sales/daily?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### 47. The super admin: platform commission per store (orders delivered today)
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/reports/commissions?from={{today}}&to={{today}}
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}


### 48. A vendor cannot see the admin dashboard -> 403
GET {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/admin/reports/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{vendorToken}}


### ===== D. Clean up =====

### 49. Put the settings back (delivery fee 30.00, free from 299.00, minimum 99.00)
PUT {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currency": "INR",
  "deliveryFee": 30.00,
  "freeDeliveryFrom": 299.00,
  "minimumOrderValue": 99.00,
  "supportEmail": "support@grocery.com",
  "supportPhone": "1800-123-4567"
}


### 50. Switch delivery slots off again
PATCH {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/super-admin/feature-flags/DELIVERY_SLOTS
Authorization: Bearer {{superAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "enabled": false
}


### 51. delivery1 goes offline
POST {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/delivery/availability/offline
Authorization: Bearer {{partnerToken}}
